linic sit-in where her father was arrested to her involvement in a cultlike Catholic youth group, with scenes that chronicle the eight-month adventure she and her husband had in her parents' household after a decade of living on their own. Lockwood details her education of a seminarian who is also living at the rectory, tries to explain Catholicism to her husband, who is mystified by its bloodthirstiness and arcane laws, and encounters a mysterious substance on a hotel bed with her mother. Lockwood pivots from the raunchy to the sublime, from the comic to the deeply serious, exploring issues of belief, belonging, and personhood. Priestdaddy is an entertaining, unforgettable portrait of a deeply odd religious upbringing, and how one balances a hard-won identity with the weight of family and tradition.","subjectCategories":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Family","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-priestdaddy-a-memoir-patricia-lockwood"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Biography","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-priestdaddy-a-memoir-patricia-lockwood"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"American Authors","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-priestdaddy-a-memoir-patricia-lockwood"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"American Poets","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-priestdaddy-a-memoir-patricia-lockwood"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Women poets","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-priestdaddy-a-memoir-patricia-lockwood"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Authors, american","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-priestdaddy-a-memoir-patricia-lockwood"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Authors, biography","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-priestdaddy-a-memoir-patricia-lockwood"},{"source":"open_library","scheme